done: 3 atoms emitted; commit=cc87d18; scale-flash root-caused + fixed (canvas layer), routeEdges wired on 5 canvases, regression e2e added

**Part A** (commit 47a51b1): The flash was `CytoscapeCanvas.tsx:1683` reading the *canvas prop* `animate` for the routeEdges defer gate. `ScaleSurface` sets `layoutOptions.animate:false` for its cached-positions preset return path, but the canvas prop stays `true` (from `!reducedMotion`), so the gate deferred routing by `animationDuration+16ms = 416ms` — straight beziers repainted for that window then snapped to routed polylines. Fix reads effective animate (`layoutOptions.animate ?? animate`); `false` and `"end"` both route synchronously at layoutstop. Added `layoutSettledRef` per-cy so the prop-change effect at line 1867 no longer routes against still-animating fresh-fcose positions on first-visit (secondary flash source). Regression probe at `tests/e2e/scale-flash.spec.ts` — publishes the Scale canvas + asserts `_segDist` bypass data is present within a window that a regression would miss without a `waitForTimeout` bump.

**Part B** (commit cc87d18): `routeEdges` enabled on all 4 ontology-workbench canvases + the RDF 1.2 shell; default 600-edge cap suffices for those demo datasets.

**Constraint gap:** Playwright browsers are not installed in this worker environment, so I could not capture the frame-pair repro artifact the brief specified as mandatory. Root cause was determined by code-level trace (specific line, specific value flow) and the regression e2e encodes the causal claim testably; CI will run the probe. `pnpm run gates` was blocked by a pnpm store lock error under sandbox (`unable to open database file`), so I ran the underlying tools directly: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `eslint src/ packages/ tests/` 0 errors (13 pre-existing warnings), `vitest run` full suite 1679 passed / 6 skipped, `prettier --check` clean after autofix.
